// provisioning critical path and are intentionally allowed to fail the whole run.
// Checkpoints are not a nice-to-have: they are the audit trail and provenance for
// any run that modifies code, and we cannot know at provision time whether a given
// run will end up modifying code. So if the CLI can't be installed, the checkpoint
// base can't be fetched, or enable fails, the run must not proceed rather than
